%N A399299 Numbers that cannot be obtained by removing the first and last digits of a square.
%C A399299 Leading 0s are disallowed, so 16 is included even though 142^2 = 20164, for example.
%H A399299 Eric Fox, <a href="/A399299/b399299.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A399299 16 is included in this sequence because it is not the center of any 4-digit square.
%e A399299 371 is excluded from this sequence because 154^2 = 23716.
%o A399299 (Python)
%o A399299 from math import isqrt
%o A399299 def ok(n):
%o A399299     s=str(n); lo=isqrt(10**(len(s)+1)-1)+1; hi=isqrt(10**(len(s)+2)-1)
%o A399299     return not any(str(k*k)[1:-1]==s for k in range(lo,hi+1))
%o A399299 print([n for n in range(1000) if ok(n)])
%o A399299 (Python)
%o A399299 from math import isqrt
%o A399299 def issquare(n):
%o A399299     return isqrt(n)**2 == n
%o A399299 def ok(n):
%o A399299     s = str(n)
%o A399299     return not any(issquare(int(c+s+d)) for c in "123456789" for d in "014569")
%o A399299 print([k for k in range(1000) if ok(k)]) # _Michael S. Branicky_, Sep 24 2026
